# Test: a peer's NOTIFICATION leaves one WARN line saying why, at the default level
# AC: spec-bgp-open-session-rfc-defects AC-3n and the log path of AC-3 (D3,
# plan/journal/silent-fall-through.md)
# Exercises: ze-peer sends NOTIFICATION OPEN Message Error / Unspecific (2/0)
# -> Session.handleNotification -> logNotificationReceived -> one
# `notification received` WARN naming the peer, the FSM state, and the code
# and subcode as names and numbers. No ze.log override: the line is visible at
# the default WARN level, which is the whole point (before D3 the reason reached
# only the counters and `show errors`).
#
# ze-peer cannot refuse ze's OPEN: `action=send` fires after its own
# OPEN/KEEPALIVE handshake (seq=1 is the first message after it), so ze reads
# the 2/0 in ESTABLISHED. The same line in OpenSent/OpenConfirm is proved by
# TestHandleNotificationLogsWarn and by the frr-software-version interop
# scenario, where FRR refuses ze's OPEN for real.

# ze-peer: after the handshake, send a raw NOTIFICATION 2/0.
# Marker (16 x FF), length 21 (0x0015), type 3, code 2, subcode 0.
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
action=send:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0015030200
EOF_PEER

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast {
					prefix {
						maximum 10000
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
await=stderr:contains=msg="notification received":then=stop
expect=stderr:pattern=level=WARN msg="notification received" subsystem=bgp\.reactor\.session peer=127\.0\.0\.1 state=ESTABLISHED code="OPEN Message Error" code-number=2 subcode=Unspecific subcode-number=0
